  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NESA Center Executive Seminar 02-23</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This course seeks to discuss the complexity of maritime security throughout the NESA region, as well as provide opportunities to discuss better methodologies for maritime cooperation and information sharing. Much of the world still suffers from sea blindness, or a lack of understanding of the degree by which challenges at sea create problems on land. This program dives into the numerous challenges in the maritime domain, including those created by states, non-state actors, or even the sea itself. The program also focuses on how the maritime community is crafting responses to these challenges from technological tools being integrated into navies and coast guards, cooperative efforts among like-minded nations, and stronger interaction between governments, commercial entities, academics, and researchers.</narrative>
  </description>
